// Title: Network Connection Initiated To Visual Studio Code Tunnels Domain
// Sigma ID: 4b657234-038e-4ad5-997c-4be42340bce4
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Kamran Saifullah
// Date: 2023-11-20 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: exfiltration, command-and-control, T1567, T1572
// Description: Detects network connections to Visual Studio Code tunnel domains initiated by a process on a
//   system. Attackers can abuse that feature to establish a reverse shell or persistence on a
//   machine.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use of Visual Studio Code tunnel will also trigger this.
// References:
//   - https://ipfyx.fr/post/visual-studio-code-tunnel/
//   - https://badoption.eu/blog/2023/01/31/code_c2.html
//   - https://cydefops.com/vscode-data-exfiltration
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/network_connection/net_connection_win_domain_vscode_tunnel_connection.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceNetworkEvents
| where RemoteUrl endswith ".tunnels.api.visualstudio.com"
